{
  "schema": "perch-native-parity-fixture/1",
  "screen": "launcher",
  "note": "Floating screen: it is drawn through a portal into the page body and placed against the window, so the reference is the whole default 1280x800 window on the app's backdrop and every box is in window coordinates. The centred, keyboard-only New session picker (stock-ui/launcher; Cmd+Shift+T or the sidebar's New session). It first lists the host's projects (and Add project and No project), then, after one is picked, that project's agents and the browser and file rows. Props are `LauncherProps` as components/NewSessionDialog.tsx builds them (the host's non-Quickchat projects with the workspace a tab would land in; `activeProjectId` is the project on screen, which starts highlighted); callbacks are no-ops. Which stage is shown, the filter text and the highlight are the screen's own state, so states reach them with `steps` (click a row = Enter on it; type into the filter). The agents come from @perch/sdk `useAgentChoices(hostId)` over the store's `agentManifestsByHost` (recorded in sdk.agentChoices). The panel is `min(480px, 100vw - 2rem)` wide, at most `min(420px, 100dvh - 16vh - 2rem)` high, 12vh down from the top.",
  "dataFrom": "sidebar",
  "size": {
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 800
  },
  "window": {
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 800
  },
